tatus":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Health and Adult Social Care Scrutiny Board","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Cabinet Petitions Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Economy, Skills, Transport and Environment Scrutiny Board","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"New Cemetery West Bromwich scheme (\u00a33.5m) completely removed from capital programme with no explanation.","lead":"The unexplained withdrawal of a \u00a33.5m capital scheme raises questions about capital planning discipline, underlying project issues, or unplanned budget pressures. Lack of transparency on scheme changes affects confidence in the council's capital governance\u2026","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Appendix 5 - General Fund Capital Programme","paper_url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35924/35924.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Disabled Facilities Grants programme cannot recover from prior-year slippage despite bringing forward \u00a34.6m.","lead":"Disabled Facilities Grants are a statutory service for elderly and disabled residents. Persistent underdelivery over multiple years indicates operational capacity constraints or process issues within the council's housing function, which is a risk\u2026","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Appendix 5 - General Fund Capital Programme","paper_url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35924/35924.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Capital programme projected to underspend by \u00a313.2m, representing 13% of revised budget.","lead":"A 13% projected underspend indicates significant execution risk on the capital programme. Delayed capital delivery affects planned service improvements and infrastructure, and suggests potential capacity or governance issues in project delivery that would\u2026","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Appendix 5 - General Fund Capital Programme","paper_url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35924/35924.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 5 - General Fund Capital Programme","paper_url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35924/35924.pdf","headline":"New Cemetery West Bromwich scheme (\u00a33.5m) completely removed from capital programme with no explanation.","detail":"The New Cemetery scheme was revised to a budget of \u00a33.5m in Q1 but shows a complete variance of (\u00a33.5m), indicating removal or deferral from the 2026/27 programme. The capital monitoring document provides no explanation for the removal of this material capital scheme.","category":"capital","matters":"The unexplained withdrawal of a \u00a33.5m capital scheme raises questions about capital planning discipline, underlying project issues, or unplanned budget pressures. Lack of transparency on scheme changes affects confidence in the council's capital governance and financial planning.","figures":"Base Budget \u00a33,353k; Slippage \u00a3127k; Revised Budget at Q1 \u00a33,480k; Variance (\u00a33,480k)","quote":"New Cemetery - West Bromwich 3,353 127 3,480 3,480 - - (3,480)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 5 - General Fund Capital Programme","paper_url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35924/35924.pdf","headline":"Disabled Facilities Grants programme cannot recover from prior-year slippage despite bringing forward \u00a34.6m.","detail":"The budget for DFGs includes \u00a34.6m carried forward from 2025/26 to address prior-year underdelivery, resulting in a total revised budget of \u00a311.5m. However, forecast expenditure is only \u00a35.5m, creating a variance of (\u00a36.0m). This indicates the council cannot deliver both the prior-year backlog and current-year demand, suggesting delivery capacity constraints.","category":"demand","matters":"Disabled Facilities Grants are a statutory service for elderly and disabled residents. Persistent underdelivery over multiple years indicates operational capacity constraints or process issues within the council's housing function, which is a risk indicator for the council's ability to meet statutory obligations and manage service demand.","figures":"Revised Budget \u00a311,478k; Forecast Expenditure \u00a35,500k; Variance (\u00a35,978k); Prior-year slippage brought forward \u00a34,607k","quote":"Disabled Facilities Grants 6,871 4,607 11,478 11,478 657 5,500 (5,978)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 5 - General Fund Capital Programme","paper_url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35924/35924.pdf","headline":"Capital programme projected to underspend by \u00a313.2m, representing 13% of revised budget.","detail":"The Grand Total shows a revised budget at Quarter 1 of \u00a398.9m but forecast expenditure of only \u00a385.7m, resulting in a variance of (\u00a313.2m). With only 10% of spend completed in Quarter 1, the projected underspend is material and spread across multiple directorates, with only Children and Education forecasting on-budget delivery.","category":"capital","matters":"A 13% projected underspend indicates significant execution risk on the capital programme. Delayed capital delivery affects planned service improvements and infrastructure, and suggests potential capacity or governance issues in project delivery that would concern lenders assessing the council's financial management.","figures":"Revised Budget at Quarter 1 \u00a398,919k; Forecast Expenditure \u00a385,683k; Forecast Outturn Variance (\u00a313,236k)","quote":"Grand Total 70,848 24,429 3,330 312 0 98,919 9,721 10% 85,683 (13,236)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 8 - Collection Fund Monitoring","paper_url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35927/35927.pdf","headline":"Net business rates income is \u00a35.2m below original forecast due to rateable value adjustments from successful business appeals","detail":"Quarter 1 forecast indicates net business rates income will be \u00a35.2m lower than the original NNDR1 estimate, driven by rateable value adjustments made by the Valuation Office following successful business appeals with refunds backdated to 2023/24. The council states much of this variance is covered by appeals provisions already set aside, and notes the underlying rateable value reduction of \u00a30.4m is not material enough to warrant Medium-Term Financial Plan adjustments, though it will be monitored.","category":"income","matters":"A \u00a35.2m variance indicates significant exposure to business appeals and rating revaluations; while the council indicates provisions cover most of this, sustained appeals activity requires monitoring to ensure provisions remain adequate","figures":"\u00a35.2m lower net business rates income; \u00a30.4m underlying rateable value reduction; gross business rates payable variance (\u00a35.2)m","quote":"The data presented indicates that net business rates income is \u00a35.2m lower than original estimates.  Much of this relates to adjustments in Rateable Value, as determined by the Valuation Office following appeals lodged by businesses.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 8 - Collection Fund Monitoring","paper_url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35927/35927.pdf","headline":"April 2025 LCTRS change introduces new council tax liabilities for previously exempt households, creating collection risk","detail":"Changes to the Local Council Tax Reduction Scheme from April 2025 mean households previously not liable for council tax are now required to contribute. The paper explicitly flags this as presenting 'a risk to council tax collection rates, which continues to be monitored.' Collection behavior of these newly liable populations is unknown and could compound the existing declining collection trend.","category":"income","matters":"Policy changes introducing newly liable populations with unproven payment behavior create forecasting uncertainty and downside risk to income, particularly when overall collection rates are already declining","figures":"Affects portion of approximately \u00a3189m total council tax liability issued","quote":"From April 2025, a change was made to the Local Council Tax Reduction Scheme (LCTRS), meaning that some households who were not liable to pay council tax in previous years are now liable to pay a contribution towards their council tax.  This presents a risk to council tax collection rates, which continues to be monitored.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-09"},"name":"Sandwell","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"New Cemetery West Bromwich scheme (\u00a33.5m) completely removed from capital programme with no explanation.","lead":"The unexplained withdrawal of a \u00a33.5m capital scheme raises questions about capital planning discipline, underlying project issues, or unplanned budget pressures. Lack of transparency on scheme changes affects confidence in the council's capital governance\u2026","also":["21 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Cabinet on 2026-10-14","n_findings":22,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 5 - General Fund Capital Programme","top_paper_url":"https://sandwell.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s35924/35924.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":110,"news_drafts_total":3}}